quran[29]{c,v,t}:
  37,154,What is the matter with you? How do you judge (things)?
  37,155,Will you not then be mindful of advice?
  37,156,Do you have (any) clear authority (to prove your accusation)?
  37,157,"Then, produce your scripture if you are truthful."
  37,158,They also claim that He has kinship with the jinn. Yet the jinn (themselves) know they will be presented (before Him for judgement).
  37,159,Allah is far above whatever they attribute (to Him).
  37,160,But the chosen servants of Allah (do not say such things).
  37,161,"Indeed, neither you nor whatever you worship,"
  37,162,"you can never tempt anyone against Him,"
  37,163,except someone who is to burn in the Hellfire.
  37,164,And (the angels say:) ‘There is none among us but has an assigned station (of worship).
  37,165,"We are, indeed, the ones ranged in ranks."
  37,166,"And surely, we are the ones (constantly) glorifying His praise.’"
  37,167,"And indeed, they (the pagans of Mecca) used to say:"
  37,168,"‘If only we had a Reminder from the ancients,"
  37,169,we would surely have been chosen servants of Allah.’
  37,170,But they disbelieve in it (now when it has come to them). So they will soon know (their end).
  37,171,"Indeed, Our Word has already gone forth in favour of Our servants, the messengers,"
  37,172,that they will surely be the supported ones.
  37,173,"And indeed, Our forces will be the victors."
  37,174,"So turn away from them for a while,"
  37,175,and watch them. So they will soon see (what happens to them).
  37,176,Do they seek to hasten Our punishment?
  37,177,"But when it descends on their courtyards, it will be a terrible morning for those (already) warned!"
  37,178,"So turn away from them for a while,"
  37,179,and watch them. So they will soon see (what happens to them).
  37,180,"Glory be to your Lord, the Lord of Might. (He is) far above whatever they attribute (to Him)."
  37,181,Peace be upon the messengers!
  37,182,"And all praise belongs to Allah, the Lord of all worlds."
